// Markdown: one document, rendered as ordinary elements. The headings, lists,
// code block, quote and table below are all built from the Markdown component's
// source, so scrolling, theming and selection are the same as anywhere else.

Column {
	id:             pageMarkdown
	visible:        false
	scroll:         true
	spacing:        24
	padding:        20
	crossAxisAlign: start
	scrollShadow:   true

	Column {
		spacing: 4
		width:   560

		Text {
			text: "Markdown"
			role: "titleMedium"
		}

		Markdown {
			id:    mdSample
			width: 560
			text:  "# A document\n\nEvery block becomes an element: a heading is a `Text` with a role, this paragraph wraps, and **bold** or [links](https://goi.dev) keep their words.\n\n## Lists\n\n- a bullet\n- another, with a nested run\n  - nested items indent\n  - by their depth\n\n1. ordered items\n2. keep the number\n\n## Code and quotes\n\n```go\nfunc main() {\n\tfmt.Println(\"rendered as a Code block\")\n}\n```\n\n> A quote gets a bar on the left, drawn by a border on the Column that holds it.\n\n---\n\n| property | type | notes |\n|---|---:|---|\n| text | string | the whole document |\n| scroll | bool | a long document scrolls its Column |\n"
		}
	}
}
